WEBVTT

00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:24.182
[MAN BREATHING FAINTLY]

00:00:35.569 --> 00:00:37.946
DUMBLEDORE:
You can't help. Harry...

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:41.825
...you wonderful boy.

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:46.204
You brave, brave man.

00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:50.167
Let us walk.

00:00:57.632 --> 00:00:59.885
Professor, what is that?

00:01:02.554 --> 00:01:05.599
Something beyond either of our help.

00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:11.730
A part of Voldemort sent here to die.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.315
And exactly where are we?

00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:18.695
I was going to ask you that.
Where would you say that we are?

00:01:18.737 --> 00:01:20.572
Well...

00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:23.241
...it looks like King's Cross station.

00:01:23.575 --> 00:01:26.036
Only cleaner.

00:01:26.077 --> 00:01:28.288
And without all the trains.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:31.583
King's Cross, is that right?

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:35.504
This is, as they say, your party.

00:01:36.671 --> 00:01:39.800
I expect you now realize
that you and Voldemort...

00:01:39.841 --> 00:01:42.803
...have been connected by something
other than fate...

00:01:42.844 --> 00:01:46.014
...since that night in Godric's Hollow
all those years ago.

00:01:46.056 --> 00:01:47.891
So it's true then, sir?

00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:50.936
A part of him lives within me, doesn't it?

00:01:51.269 --> 00:01:52.395
Did.

00:01:52.437 --> 00:01:57.275
It was just destroyed many moments ago
by none other than Voldemort himself.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:03.031
You were the Horcrux
he never meant to make, Harry.

00:02:15.585 --> 00:02:17.254
I have to go back, haven't I?

00:02:17.295 --> 00:02:19.297
Oh. That's up to you.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.258
I have a choice?

00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:23.218
Oh, yes.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.096
We're in King's Cross, you say?

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.977
I think, if you so desired,
you'd be able to board a train.

00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:34.855
And where would it take me?

00:02:34.896 --> 00:02:36.273
[DUMBLEDORE CHUCKLES]

00:02:36.314 --> 00:02:38.149
On.

00:02:40.569 --> 00:02:43.113
[TRAIN WHISTLE WAILS IN DISTANCE]

00:02:56.126 --> 00:02:58.211
Voldemort has the Elder Wand.

00:03:00.839 --> 00:03:02.007
True.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.968
-And the snake's still alive.
-Yes.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.596
And I've nothing to kill it with.

00:03:08.138 --> 00:03:12.851
Help will always be given at Hogwarts,
Harry, to those who ask for it.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.772
I've always prized myself
on my ability to turn a phrase.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.985
Words are,
in my not so humble opinion...

00:03:22.027 --> 00:03:25.739
...our most inexhaustible
source of magic...

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:30.118
...capable of both inflicting injury
and remedying it.

00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:36.666
But I would, in this case,
amend my original statement to this:

00:03:39.461 --> 00:03:45.634
Help will always be given at Hogwarts
to those who deserve it.

00:03:51.473 --> 00:03:54.225
Do not pity the dead, Harry.

00:03:54.684 --> 00:03:56.728
Pity the living.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:02.150
And, above all,
all those who live without love.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:08.531
Professor, my mother's Patronus
was a doe, wasn't it?

00:04:09.574 --> 00:04:12.202
That's the same as Professor Snape's.

00:04:13.078 --> 00:04:15.288
It's curious, don't you think?

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:20.293
Actually, if I think about it,
it doesn't seem curious at all.

00:04:22.003 --> 00:04:24.172
I'll be going now, Harry.

00:04:24.714 --> 00:04:26.049
Professor?

00:04:30.553 --> 00:04:32.722
Is this all real?

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.350
Or is it just happening inside my head?

00:04:35.392 --> 00:04:39.062
Of course it's happening inside
your head, Harry.

00:04:39.104 --> 00:04:42.857
Why should that mean that it's not real?

00:04:48.446 --> 00:04:51.074
Professor? What should I do?

00:04:55.787 --> 00:04:57.580
Professor?

00:05:00.959 --> 00:05:02.377
BELLATRIX:
My Lord?

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:04.671
My Lord, are you hurt? My Lord?

00:05:04.713 --> 00:05:06.464
I don't need your help.

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:09.217
BELLATRIX:
No. Come.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.894
The boy.

00:05:19.936 --> 00:05:21.855
Is he dead?

00:05:35.952 --> 00:05:38.288
[WHISPERS]
Is he alive?

00:05:38.329 --> 00:05:40.498
Draco, is he alive?

00:06:07.192 --> 00:06:08.693
Dead.

